SkyWell – 7-Day MVP Plan (MVP-Only Version)

Goal:
Build a data-focused MVP app that fetches CAMS and Open-Meteo data for Berlin, calculates personalized environmental risk scores, and returns natural-language recommendations via a Gradio chatbot interface. The MVP mimics production architecture with Docker, Redis, FastAPI, Jinja2, and GitHub Actions (CI/CD).

Day 1 – ETL Bootstrap & DevOps Setup
- Scaffold repo and folders (etl/, core/, api/, ui/, tests/, .github/workflows/)
- Create .env.example for API keys
- Write etl/fetch.py to download today + 3-day CAMS air quality forecast for Berlin
- Write etl/fetch_uv.py to download 4-day UV forecast via Open-Meteo API
- Add Dockerfile for ETL
- Add GitHub Actions workflow (etl.yml) to run ETL daily
- Add Docker Compose (docker-compose.yml) for local orchestration
- Add Redis service to docker-compose.yml for caching

Day 2 – Grid Harmonisation
- Implement core/grid.py to reproject CAMS/UV data to 0.01° grid (using xarray)
- Store harmonized output as Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFFs in data/
- Write helper load_grid(date) to read datasets
- Update Docker Compose to include all services (ETL, Redis, API)

Day 3 – Risk & Advice Logic
- Implement core/risk.py: normalization, risk vector computation
- Implement core/advice.py: rule-based mapping of risk values to advice (8–10 categories)
- Add tests/test_risk.py
- Add Dockerfile for backend (FastAPI)
- Implement choose_advice() function
- Add tests/test_risk.py
- Add Dockerfile for backend (FastAPI)

Day 4 – REST API & Chatbot Script
- Implement api/main.py using FastAPI
- /risk: returns numeric risk vector as JSON
- /chat: returns rendered advice sentence via Jinja2
- Implement api/cache.py with Redis for caching responses
- Add chatbot/templates/ for Jinja2 templates
- Add tests/test_api.py
- Update Docker Compose with API + Redis

Day 5 – UI with Gradio
- Implement ui/app.py using Gradio:
- Form for health profile and date selection
- Calls /risk and /chat endpoints
- Displays personalized advice
- Add Dockerfile for UI
- Add README.md with run/deploy instructions
- Add Makefile or run_all.sh to launch API + UI together
-Calls /risk and /chat endpoints
-Displays personalized advice
-Add Dockerfile for UI
-Add README.md with run/deploy instructions
-Add Makefile or run_all.sh to launch API + UI together

Day 6 – Polish, Test & CI/CD
- Format code with black, lint with ruff
- Finalize README.md
- Add integration tests for API
- Add GitHub Actions workflow (ci.yml) for lint/test/build/ETL
- Set up .env management
-Add integration tests for API
-Add GitHub Actions workflow (ci.yml) for lint/test/build/ETL
-Set up .env management

Day 7 – Deploy & Demo
- Push to GitHub
- Deploy backend + UI (e.g. on Render.com using Docker)
- Schedule ETL as cron job on Render
- Record demo video

